# Exam track — Theme: Vacation & Travel — Sub-lesson 3: Talking About It
# @question sentences: the examiner asks in Luxembourgish, the learner
# assembles the Luxembourgish answer (always en→lu).

@lesson V1.03 "Talking About Vacation"

@sentence
@question Wou fuert Dir dëst Joer an d'Vakanz?
@lu Dëst Joer fuere mir a Frankräich.
@en This year we are going to France.
@distractor-lu gëschter
@distractor-lu waren

@sentence
@question Wéi reest Dir am léifsten?
@lu Ech reesen am léifste mam Zuch.
@en I like traveling by train the most.
@distractor-lu Fliger
@distractor-lu ni

@sentence
@question Wat war Är schéinste Vakanz?
@lu Meng schéinste Vakanz war an Italien.
@en My most beautiful vacation was in Italy.
@distractor-lu wäert
@distractor-lu sinn

@sentence
@question Wat maacht Dir gär an der Vakanz?
@lu Ech gi gär op d'Plage schwammen.
@en I like to go swimming at the beach.
@distractor-lu schaffen
@distractor-lu ni

@sentence
@question Mat wiem fuert Dir an d'Vakanz?
@lu Ech fuere mat menger Famill an d'Vakanz.
@en I go on vacation with my family.
@distractor-lu eleng
@distractor-lu ouni

@sentence
@question Wéi laang bleift Dir do?
@lu Mir bleiwen zwou Wochen do.
@en We are staying there for two weeks.
@distractor-lu Deeg
@distractor-lu eng

@sentence
@question Wat huelt Dir mat an d'Vakanz?
@lu Ech huele meng Valise a mäi Pass mat.
@en I take my suitcase and my passport with me.
@distractor-lu deng
@distractor-lu ouni

@sentence
@question Wéi ass d'Wieder op der Plage?
@lu D'Wieder ass waarm an d'Sonn schéngt.
@en The weather is warm and the sun is shining.
@distractor-lu kal
@distractor-lu reent
